This is an additive component of the same Poincare formalization project.

Eight cap-filling and closed-cover source files are preserved byte-for-byte
from KunHcz/poincare-lean@c0695e2e2ca9f7ffead14675b80fdddd3dcc01eb.
Their repeated declarations are not counted as new contributions.

Mathlib supplies the real-to-additive-circle covering, covering lifts and
their uniqueness, compact-support zero extension, quotient topology and
path-component machinery. Their authors retain their attribution. The
proof of simple connectivity of the standard two-sphere used in the
concrete model belongs to the pinned HatcherLib reference formalization at
bb91a091f0b968f8bbe8d861e025a88d82b161be, not to this new component.

The local contribution constructs the concrete collar crossing map,
normalizes its global real lift, derives the separating path-connected
regions and connects them to actual capping, with a full-input compact
cylinder regression. These are classical topological facts, not claims
of a new mathematical discovery or complete Poincare formalization.

